BT 1 0 0 1 0 62.5 Tm 14.5 TL /F2 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg (Problem:) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( an IP address has two roles - identifying a host and indicating its location \(the network prefix\).) Tj T* (When a device moves to another network its address no longer matches the local prefix, so packets are) Tj T* (routed to the old network and the device would need a new address, which breaks ongoing TCP) Tj T* (connections. ) Tj /F2 10 Tf (Mobile IP) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( \(RFC 5944 for IPv4\) lets a device keep its permanent address while moving, so) Tj T* (applications are not interrupted.) Tj T* ET
