BT 1 0 0 1 0 48 Tm 14.5 TL /F2 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg (Observation:) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( For frames sent by the host to the internet, the destination MAC is that of the default) Tj T* (gateway \(router\), not the remote server, because MAC addresses are only meaningful within one link.) Tj T* (ARP requests use the broadcast destination FF:FF:FF:FF:FF:FF, while replies are unicast. The first three) Tj T* (bytes \(OUI\) of each MAC identify the NIC vendor.) Tj T* ET
